      "reason_code": "evidence_supports_claim",
      "claim": "The Flamingo pipeline consists of: a pretrained vision encoder (NFNet F6 pretrained contrastively, CLIP-style) that extracts spatial features; a Perceiver Resampler that takes image/video features and outputs a fixed-size set (64) of visual tokens; and a pretrained frozen autoregressive language model conditioned via freshly-initialized cross-attention layers (interleaved with the frozen LM layers) with gating mechanisms. These components are organized so the vision encoder feeds the Resampler, whose visual tokens condition the LM through cross-attention for next-token prediction.",
